{{!
    @template tool_vae/form_note

    A sentence a form of the plugin places between its fields: a reminder or a warning in a div, a memo in a paragraph, a
    heading. On one logical line, each break carried by a comment: the form places it as it comes.

    Every text comes from the context, worded by tool_vae\output\form_note. The template holds no logic. Every value is
    escaped (double braces): none of them is HTML.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * isdiv - bool, the sentence is in a div
    * isp - bool, the sentence is in a paragraph
    * ish3 - bool, the sentence is a heading
    * class - string, the classes of the element
    * withid - null, or {value}: the id of the element, that the fields of the form point to
    * text - string, the sentence

    Example context (json):
    {
        "isdiv": true,
        "isp": false,
        "ish3": false,
        "class": "alert alert-info tool-vae-anonymise",
        "withid": {"value": "tool_vae_anonymise"},
        "text": "Do not write the name of a person you work with."
    }
}}
{{#isdiv}}<div class="{{class}}"{{#withid}} id="{{value}}"{{/withid}}>{{text}}</div>{{/isdiv}}{{!
}}{{#isp}}<p class="{{class}}"{{#withid}} id="{{value}}"{{/withid}}>{{text}}</p>{{/isp}}{{!
}}{{#ish3}}<h3 class="{{class}}">{{text}}</h3>{{/ish3}}
